        {
          "question": "Will my parent be charged for the meals?",
          "answer": "There is no required payment statewide. Some local providers suggest or encourage a voluntary donation, but the meals are not withheld if your parent cannot or chooses not to contribute. If you are asked about payment, clarify that you are asking whether meals are available without it."
        },
        {
          "question": "My parent is in the hospital right now. Can we start the process before they come home?",
          "answer": "Yes, and it is a good idea. Call the parish Council on Aging now, explain that your parent will be returning home and will need meal delivery. Discharge planners at the hospital may also be able to initiate or support the referral. Getting on the list before discharge means less gap in care once your parent is home."
        },
        {
          "question": "What happens if my parent moves to a different parish?",
          "answer": "Enrollment in one parish does not transfer automatically. If your parent moves, you will need to contact the Council on Aging in the new parish and go through intake again. The new parish may have different meal formats, delivery schedules, or wait times. Contact the new provider as early as possible to minimize any gap in service."
        }
