      "intro": "Caring for an aging parent is a full-time responsibility that most families take on without any outside help. Louisiana's National Family Caregiver Support Program (NFCSP) exists specifically for you, the caregiver, not just your parent. Through your local Area Agency on Aging, this program can connect you with in-home respite care (temporary relief so you can rest or handle other obligations), caregiver counseling, support groups, sitter services, and educational resources.\n\nThis program is funded under the federal Older Americans Act and administered in Louisiana through the Governor's Office of Elderly Affairs and a statewide network of local aging agencies. There is no fixed income test or asset limit that disqualifies you. The key question is whether you are an active family caregiver for an older adult, or a grandparent or relative caregiver raising a child.\n\nWhat you can actually receive depends on your parish. Each local Area Agency on Aging controls its own service mix, funding levels, and intake process. Some parishes offer in-home respite directly; others refer you to partner providers. Call your local agency first to find out exactly what is available where you live.",
