        {
          "type": "callout",
          "title": "What services can you actually get?",
          "body": "Louisiana's NFCSP may provide any combination of these depending on your parish and available funding: in-home respite care (someone comes to your home so you can take a break), group respite, caregiver sitter services, individual counseling, caregiver support groups, public education and training, and information and assistance connecting you with other resources. No single parish offers all of these at all times. Your local agency will tell you what is currently available."
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "title": "Why services vary by parish",
          "body": "The NFCSP is a federally funded program under the Older Americans Act, but Louisiana administers it through a network of local Area Agencies on Aging. Each agency receives a portion of state and federal funding and decides which services to offer based on local need and capacity. This means two caregivers in different parishes may receive different services, face different wait times, or go through different intake processes. The Governor's Office of Elderly Affairs at (225) 342-7100 can tell you which Area Agency on Aging covers your parish."
        }
